   <td>IBETO</td>\n                <td>₦1,645.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>GULF TREASURE</td>\n                <td>₦1,645.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>TMDK</td>\n                <td>₦1,645.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>NIPCO WARRI</td>\n                <td>₦1,705.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MENJ</td>\n                <td>₦1,700.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>INTERGRATED</td>\n                <td>₦1,645.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBACHEM</td>\n                <td>₦1,645.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DUPORT</td>\n                <td>₦1,645.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Drop Nearly 7% as Brent Falls to $90 on Iran Truce Hopes\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Global oil prices fell nearly 7 percent on Monday, dragging Brent crude down to $90 per barrel. The decline reflects growing optimism that diplomatic efforts could prevent a wider regional conflict. Despite the sharp fall in crude prices, energy markets remain cautious as major shipping routes continue to face operational risks.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-drop-nearly-7-as-brent-falls-to-90-on-iran-truce-hopes\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Dangote Says Naira Petrol Sales Resumed to Prevent Fuel Scarcity\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Dangote Petroleum Refinery has disclosed that its decision to resume the sale of Premium Motor Spirit (PMS) in naira was driven by the need to avert a potential fuel shortage. A senior management official of the refinery, who spoke on condition of anonymity, said the decision was taken to stabilise the domestic market. The disclosure comes days after the refinery abandoned its short-lived dollar-denominated pricing regime.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/dangote-says-naira-petrol-sales-resumed-to-prevent-fuel-scarcity\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Vessel Arrivals: AA Rano, Nepal, NIPCO, Others Receive Fresh PMS, AGO Cargoes\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Fresh cargoes of Premium Motor Spirit (PMS), and Automotive Gas Oil (AGO) are continuing to arrive at key petroleum depots across Lagos, Warri and Calabar. The latest tanker position report monitored by Petroleumprice.ng shows multiple vessels either discharging, awaiting berth or scheduled to commence discharge between July 22 and July 25.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/vessel-arrivals-aa-rano-nepal-nipco-others-receive-fresh-pms-ago-cargoes\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Sink 5% After U.S-Iran Pause Military Attacks\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Global oil prices retreated sharply on Monday after the United States and Iran suspended hostilities. Brent crude was trading at US$92.41 per barrel, down 4.52 per cent. West Texas Intermediate (WTI) fell 4.79 per cent to US$85.03 per barrel.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-sink-5-after-us-iran-pause-military-attacks\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Strait of Hormuz Reopening Talks Gain Momentum as Oman Leads Fresh Iran Diplomacy\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Oman and Iran held high-level discussions aimed at restoring navigation through one of the world's most strategic oil shipping routes. Washington has suspended air strikes on Iran for two consecutive nights. Iran also announced that it has suspended retaliatory attacks against U.S. allies.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/strait-of-hormuz-reopening-talks-gain-momentum-as-oman-leads-fresh-iran-diplomacy\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
